# Where the environment comes from.
#
# Committed per-mode defaults:
#   .env.development   the dashboard on localhost, used by `pnpm dev`
#   .env.production    the deployed dashboard, used by `pnpm build`
#
# Local overrides, ignored by git. Highest precedence first, verified against
# this project's Vite version:
#   .env.development.local   development only  — point at another port or host
#   .env.production.local    production builds only
#   .env.local
#   .env
#
# VITE_API_URL points at /api/v1/account/prices in each build mode.
# VITE_WEB_URL points to the same website whose session cookie authenticates
# VITE_API_URL: localhost:3000 in development, pricehistory.id in production.
# The extension uses the signed-in website session, never a bundled bearer.
# With no session or an unavailable API, price observations remain local.
# Legacy sync_queue entries remain local and are never uploaded automatically.
